        "english": "An incisive observation. In Sōseki's third-person novels — 'And Then,' 'The Gate' and others — there is to-and-fro between ground text and character consciousness, but it does not reach complete dissolution. Fully free-indirect-discourse prose, one might say, comes to fruition in the postwar Abe Kōbō and Ōe."
