    "register_notes": "Reception history / canon studies ở C2 Japanese requires fluent integration của German reception aesthetics, French sociology of literature, và Anglo-American canon debates. (1) GERMAN RECEPTION AESTHETICS — ヤウス (Jauss) 受容美学, 期待の地平 (horizon of expectations), 美的経験の歴史性 (historicity of aesthetic experience). イーザー (Iser) implied reader, blanks/gaps reader fills. Imported into Japan 1980s. Foundation. (2) FRENCH SOCIOLOGY OF LITERATURE — ブルデュー (Bourdieu) 文学場 (literary field), 文化資本 (cultural capital), 卓越化 (distinction). Allows analyzing how literary value produced through institutional positions, not text-immanent. (3) AMERICAN CANON DEBATES — 1980s-90s 'culture wars' debate over Western canon (Bloom defending vs Lauter, Smith critiquing). Less directly imported into Japan but provided reference frame for Japanese decanonization debates. (4) JAPANESE-SPECIFIC RECEPTION ISSUES — 国民文学 (national literature) construction trong Meiji era; Iwanami Shoten 全集 publishing as canonization mechanism; postwar 国語教科書 (national language textbooks) reproducing canon; 文学賞 system (Akutagawa, Naoki, Mishima, etc.) as contemporary canon-formation. C2 critic addresses all these institutional layers. (5) MARGINALIZED CATEGORIES — women writers (田村俊子, 林芙美子, 大田洋子), colonial-origin Japanese-language writers (朝鮮、台湾), popular literature (講談, 新派劇, 流行小説), Okinawan literature, Buraku literature. Each requires specific scholarship engagement. Analytical moves. (1) PERIODIZE RECEPTION — divide reception history into phases với clear historical markers. Each phase has dominant interpretive frame. (2) IDENTIFY MEDIATING INSTITUTIONS — for each phase, what publishers, critics, educational institutions, prizes mediated reception? (3) RECOVER MARGINALIZED READINGS — what interpretations were available in earlier phases that later phases foreclosed? (4) DENATURALIZE CURRENT CANON — show how present canonical positioning is contingent historical product, không essential. (5) AVOID PRESENTIST PROJECTION — không assume current dominant reading was always operative. Distinct historical readings deserve their own reconstruction. Forbidden moves: 'X is a great work' (canonical assumption smuggled in); 'X has always been recognized' (presentist false); 'X was rediscovered' (passive voice obscures rediscoverers). Required: explicit historicization of valuation, identification of valuating agents, attention to what valuation excludes. Critic to read: ヤウス『挑発としての文学史』, イーザー『行為としての読書』, ブルデュー『芸術の規則』, 鈴木貞美『「日本文学」の成立』, 安藤宏 私小説 institutional history.",
