    "cultural_notes_vi": "Canon studies ở Japanese tradition has 4 distinguishing features. (1) IWANAMI SHOTEN AS CANONIZER — 岩波書店 publishing house functions như semi-official canon-forming institution. 岩波文庫 inclusion confers canonical status. 全集 (collected works) published by Iwanami particularly weighty. C2 critic addresses publishing-institutional canon mechanism. (2) NATIONAL LANGUAGE TEXTBOOK REPRODUCTION — 中学・高校 国語 curriculum strongly canon-reproductive. Authors taught: 漱石 (forever), 鴎外, 太宰, 川端, 三島 (selectively). What's NOT taught — popular fiction, women writers' major works, colonial-era Japanese literature — equally significant. Curriculum analysis = canon analysis. (3) POSTWAR LEFT-WING CANON RECONSTRUCTION — postwar 民主主義文学 movement attempted recanonization elevating 小林多喜二 (Kobayashi Takiji), 宮本百合子 (Miyamoto Yuriko), other proletarian writers. Partial success; some entries into school curriculum. Important parallel canon-formation. (4) RECENT GENDERED RECANONIZATION — feminist scholarship since 1990s recovered 田村俊子, 平塚らいてう writings, 大田洋子 (Hiroshima literature), 林芙美子. Major institutional revaluation underway. C2 critic addresses ongoing recanonization. Khác VN: VN literary canon formation primarily state-institutional (textbook curriculum, official literary history); Japanese canon multi-mediated (publishing + criticism + education + prizes + commercial market). More dispersed authority. Mẹo: nếu bạn analyze canonical work, address its canon-status genealogy briefly. Even one paragraph showing awareness of canon-formation prevents methodologically naive reading. Mẹo về marginalized writers — recovery work requires (1) primary text access (often out of print, requires special library), (2) historical contextualization (why marginalized?), (3) interpretive frame justification (why worth recovering?). Triple challenge. Mẹo về 文学全集 (complete works editions) — what's included determines what's read. 鴎外全集 vs 漱石全集 contain editorial choices about what counts as canonical work. Editorial apparatus itself critical object. Mẹo cuối: canon studies in Japanese context unavoidably political. Decanonization positions itself as progressive; canon defense often (not always) conservative-aesthetic. Avoid taking polemical position prematurely; map debate carefully. Methodological neutrality possible while substantive position emerges from analysis.",
    "tip_advice_vi": "Workflow reception history paper C2 Japanese. (a) DEFINE OBJECT PRECISELY — 'reception of work X' too broad. Narrow: reception in era Y, by interpretive community Z, through medium W. Specificity enables manageable analysis. (b) ASSEMBLE RECEPTION SOURCES — published reviews of work in target era, literary historiography mentions, textbook inclusions, scholar interpretations, popular cultural references. Five-source minimum for substantive analysis. (c) CHRONOLOGIZE — date every reception data point. Pattern emerges: cluster moments (sudden interest), silence moments (forgetting), revaluation moments (return). Visualize timeline. (d) IDENTIFY MEDIATING AGENTS — for each reception phase, who were the critics, editors, scholars, teachers shaping reception? Names matter. Personal networks visible. (e) HISTORICIZE INTERPRETIVE FRAMES — what was era's dominant literary theory? Naturalism (Meiji)? Marxism (Taishō-Shōwa)? Existentialism (postwar)? Postmodernism (1980s)? Frame conditions reading. (f) RECONSTRUCT MARGINALIZED READINGS — which earlier readings have become invisible? Recover them. (g) STAKES-ARTICULATION — what does this reception history reveal about literary institution mechanisms generally? Beyond specific work, what is your contribution to method? Mẹo về citation pattern — reception study cite (1) one reception theorist (Jauss / Iser), (2) one literary sociology theorist (Bourdieu / Casanova), (3) Japanese institutional historians (鈴木貞美, 平岡敏夫), (4) primary reception sources (reviews, textbooks). Quadruple grounding. Mẹo về controversial canon claims — claiming X should be added to canon hoặc Y should be removed is rhetorically rich but methodologically tricky. Better: analyze the canon-formation process, leave normative implications implicit. Reader draws conclusions. Mẹo về digital methods — corpus analysis tools (NDLDigital, Aozora, 国会図書館 databases) enable reception scope mapping at scale. Frequency of mention, citation, reprint tracked computationally. Cutting-edge. Mẹo về marginalized recovery — be careful không to romanticize marginalized writer as heroically suppressed genius. Marginalization complex (sometimes work genuinely uneven; sometimes scholarship limited by archive availability; sometimes work waited for adequate readers). Methodological humility. Mẹo cuối: reception history papers risk taxonomy without analysis ('phase 1, phase 2, phase 3'). Resist. Goal là explanation: WHY each phase took form it did, WHY transitions occurred. Mechanism analysis primary.",
