    "register_notes": "Theoretical criticism ở C2 Japanese requires fluent vocabulary across 4 major lens families. (1) FORMALIST/STRUCTURALIST — ロシア・フォルマリズム (Russian Formalism), 異化 (estrangement, ostranenie), 文学性 (literariness, литературность); チェコ構造主義 (Mukařovský, Jakobson); アメリカ新批評 (New Criticism, Brooks, Empson, Wimsatt); フランス構造主義 (Lévi-Strauss, early Barthes, Genette). Often considered 'classical' apparatus, sometimes dismissed but still operative as analytical tool. (2) FEMINIST CRITICISM (3 waves, Japanese reception varied) — first-wave: rights-focused (Hiratsuka Raichō era essays). Second-wave: ガイノクリティシズム (Showalter), women's writing tradition recovery (Japanese 女流文学 revaluation, 上野千鶴子 sociological work). Third-wave: poststructural feminist theory (Butler 'gender performativity' — translated 1990s, deeply influential), クィア批評 (queer criticism). Japanese feminist literary scholarship: 与那覇恵子, 江種満子, 竹村和子 (Butler translator). (3) POSTCOLONIAL CRITICISM — サイード『オリエンタリズム』(translated 1986, foundational); スピヴァク 'Can the subaltern speak?', インターセクショナリティ; ホミ・バーバ 'mimicry', 'hybridity'. Japanese reception complicated by Japan's own colonial history (朝鮮, 台湾, 満州, 沖縄, 北海道) — postcolonial critique applied both to Japan-as-colonized (West) and Japan-as-colonizer. Important Japanese postcolonial scholars: 西川長夫, 酒井直樹, 戸邉秀明. (4) RECEPTION/READER-RESPONSE — already covered ở L108. Often cross-applied. Methodological principles. (1) THEORY ILLUMINATES, NOT DICTATES — theory should reveal patterns text contains, không impose patterns text doesn't. Test: does textual evidence support theoretically-predicted reading? If forced, theory wrong choice. (2) HISTORICIZE THEORY ITSELF — every theory products of historical moment, particular intellectual community. Apply contextually. Bringing 1970s Anglo feminist criticism unmodified to 1980s Japanese context anachronistic. (3) MULTIPLE THEORIES MEAN INTERSECTION ANALYSIS — Crenshaw's intersectionality methodologically essential khi multiple identity categories operative. Não parallel application — analyze intersection. (4) AVOID THEORETICAL ECLECTICISM AS CAMOUFLAGE — citing many theorists without committed engagement = signal of methodological insecurity, không sophistication. Better: deep engagement với 2-3 theorists than surface invocation of 10. Forbidden moves: 'X theory shows Y' bare claim — assumes theory authority without textual demonstration; 'we can apply Z theory' bare gesture — application requires textual work; theory-name-dropping без engaging concepts. Required: every theory invocation accompanied by specific concept, demonstrate concept's analytic work on specific text. Critic to read: バルト『S/Z』(formalist tour de force), ショーウォルター『女性作家』, バトラー『ジェンダー・トラブル』, サイード『オリエンタリズム』, スピヴァク『サバルタンは語ることができるか』, 上野千鶴子, 竹村和子, 酒井直樹.",
