    "cultural_notes_vi": "Theoretical criticism ở Japan có 4 đặc điểm. (1) FRENCH THEORY DOMINANCE — Japanese literary theory landscape historically dominated by French theory (Sartre 1950s-60s, structuralism 1970s, post-structuralism 1980s, Deleuze 1990s-present). German hermeneutics (Gadamer, Jauss) secondary. American new historicism, cultural studies later và less penetrative. C2 critic biết French-theory primacy. (2) BUTLER RECEPTION HUGE — Judith Butler's 'Gender Trouble' (Japanese trans 1999 by 竹村和子) had major impact on Japanese gender studies. Performativity concept widely operative. Butler-derived analysis common ở contemporary feminist literary criticism. (3) POSTCOLONIAL ASYMMETRY — Japan colonized Asian neighbors (朝鮮, 台湾, 満州, 南洋) yet was atomic-bombed by US và occupied 1945-52. Postcolonial analysis applied trong both directions. Japanese scholars must navigate complex positionality — postcolonial critique cuts both ways. 西川長夫 wrote extensively on Japan-as-colonizer; less Japanese scholarship on Japan-as-colonized vis-à-vis America. (4) THEORY-RESISTANCE TRADITION — 蓮實重彦 famously argues against systematic theoretical application. 江藤淳 was conservative-aesthetic. 加藤典洋 navigates both theoretical engagement và resistance. C2 critic engages this tradition — knowing arguments against theory enriches use of theory. Khác VN: VN literary theory Soviet-era Marxist orthodoxy followed by gradual French/American opening; Japanese trajectory more eclectic, more direct French reception, less ideological constraint. Methodological pluralism greater. Mẹo: nếu bạn deploy Butler/Spivak/Said, ALWAYS cite Japanese reception scholars (竹村和子 cho Butler, Japanese postcolonial scholars cho Said/Spivak). Direct Anglophone citation only signals incomplete grounding. Mẹo về translation issues — major theorists' Japanese translations may differ from English originals. 「サバルタン」transliteration of Spivak's term, but 「他者」 sometimes used — different connotations. C2 critic aware of translation choices. Mẹo về theoretical school affiliation — Japanese academic departments có theoretical leanings. Hitotsubashi heavy German philosophy; Tokyo French theory; Waseda comparative; Kyoto more humanistic/literary. Knowing department theoretical culture helps positioning. Mẹo cuối: theory-application papers risk becoming 'X theory + Y text' formula. Mature work makes theory itself critical object — what theory illuminates, what it occludes, how it must be modified for object. Bidirectional theory-text relation.",
    "tip_advice_vi": "Workflow theoretical criticism C2 Japanese cho luận văn / book review. (a) START FROM TEXT, NOT THEORY — read text intensively first, identify what's striking, puzzling, requiring explanation. THEN ask: which theoretical framework illuminates this puzzle? Theory chosen to fit problem, không vice versa. (b) ENGAGE 2-3 THEORISTS DEEPLY — not 10 superficially. Choose theorists whose concepts genuinely illuminate your specific text. Read them in original language plus Japanese translation. Note translation choices. (c) IDENTIFY TENSION POINTS — where does theory not fit perfectly? Don't paper over. Tension points = analytical opportunities. Maybe text resists theory; maybe theory needs modification; maybe text and theory together produce new insight. (d) APPLY-AND-MODIFY — after applying theory, ask: what about object requires modifying theory? Mature C2 work modifies theory based on textual evidence. Pure application = theory illustration; modification = theoretical contribution. (e) ETHICAL POSITIONALITY — for feminist/postcolonial/queer theory especially, articulate your own positionality vis-à-vis material. Vietnamese scholar reading Japanese colonial-era Korean literature has specific positionality requiring acknowledgment. (f) HISTORICIZE THEORY — theory contextualized in moment, place, debate. Bringing 1980s American feminism unmodified to contemporary Japanese context anachronism. Theory's own history part of analysis. Mẹo về citation pattern — theoretical paper cite (1) theorist's primary text in original or translation, (2) at least one Japanese reception scholar, (3) competing theoretical frameworks engaged briefly để show why your choice, (4) primary literary text với specific edition. Quadruple grounding. Mẹo về controversial theoretical claims — questioning canonical theory application is publishable IF carefully done. Argue against established Sōseki feminist reading; argue against established Murakami postmodern reading. Reviewer scrutinous, prepare evidence. Mẹo về intersectional analysis — when multiple identity categories matter (gender + class + ethnicity + colonial status), don't add them; analyze intersection. Crenshaw's original argument: intersection produces unique analytical object, không sum of parts. Mẹo về political tone — feminist/postcolonial criticism risks political polemic that obscures literary analysis. Maintain analytic rigor; political implications emerge from analysis, không substitute for it. Mẹo cuối: theoretical eclecticism legitimate IF justified. Pure single-framework purity rare in mature work. Most C2 essays deploy several frames opportunistically, anchored in textual question. Articulate why eclectic, không hide it.",
