    "cultural_notes_vi": "Critical essay opening conventions ở Japanese tradition khác Anglo-American ở 4 điểm. (1) HIGHER TOLERANCE FOR ALLUSIVE OPENINGS — Japanese critical essays sometimes open với literary allusion, classical citation, atmospheric scene-setting. Anglo-American academic prose generally requires explicit thesis statement at opening. C2 critic balances both. (2) LESS THESIS-DRIVEN — Anglo-American academic opening expects 'this paper argues X' explicit thesis. Japanese tradition often more inductive — opening sets question, thesis emerges through development. Pure imitation of Anglo-American thesis-statement form may feel mechanical in Japanese. (3) READER ASSUMED COMPETENT — Japanese academic prose assumes reader knows field vocabulary, major figures, basic positions. Less explanation needed at opening. Vietnamese reader trained ở Anglo-American norms may over-explain in Japanese context, signaling outsider status. (4) ESSAY VS PAPER DISTINCTION — Japanese 評論 (essay) tradition strong (柄谷, 加藤, 蓮實 published primarily essay-form). Less formal than academic 論文. C2 critic distinguishes which format target venue expects. Khác VN: VN academic essays often more thesis-explicit (French structuralist influence) than Japanese counterparts. Adjustment requires loosening explicit thesis-statement habit while maintaining intellectual rigor. Mẹo: study openings of essays in target venue trước viết. 文学界, 群像, 新潮, すばる each có distinct opening conventions. Mismatch = signals insider/outsider status. Mẹo về first-sentence importance — Japanese critical readers attend heavily to first sentence. Often determines whether reader continues. Invest disproportionate time on first sentence. Anecdote: 蓮實 reportedly rewrites first sentence dozens of times. Mẹo về 字数 — typical Japanese 評論 5000-10000 字; opening 3-paragraph section ~600-1000 字 (10-15 percent of total). Proportion guideline. Mẹo cuối: avoid two trap opening modes — (1) 'I' opening (autobiographical anecdote about how I came to this topic — too personal cho academic context); (2) 'we all know' opening (assumes consensus — patronizing, often false). Both mark amateur. Mature opening engages question directly với appropriate humility.",
    "tip_advice_vi": "Workflow opening writing C2 Japanese cho critical essay. (a) WRITE OPENING LAST — counter-intuitive but essential. Opening should reflect what paper actually accomplished. Pre-written openings drift from final argument. Draft opening, write paper, rewrite opening based on what emerged. (b) IDENTIFY MOST STRIKING TEXTUAL DETAIL — what passage/word/scene initially provoked your inquiry? That detail belongs ở opening. Concrete textual detail = best opening anchor. (c) FRAME QUESTION GENERATIVELY — question that prompts extended thought, không question with quick yes/no answer. Test: can your question be answered in one sentence? If yes, question too narrow. (d) RECONSTRUCT RECEIVED VIEW FAIRLY — even if you'll critique it, represent received view at opening accurately. Strawmen kill credibility. Spend time getting consensus right. (e) DIFFERENTIATE SPECIFICALLY — không generic 'this paper takes a new approach'. Specific: 'this paper, unlike X who emphasizes Y, attends to Z'. Specific differentiation respects readers' time. (f) THEORY AS DEMAND — theoretical commitment last in opening, framed as demanded by problem, không as pre-selected toolkit. (g) END OPENING WITH FORWARD-POINTING — last sentence of opening should preview what's coming. 'Below, after first examining〜, we proceed to〜'. Reader knows where headed. Mẹo về first-sentence templates (study, modify, don't copy): - 「〜の冒頭部における〜という細部は、しばしば看過されてきた。しかし、この一語こそが、〜の核心を孕んでいるのではないか。」(Hasumi-style detail opening) - 「もし〜ならば、〜という結論が必然的に導かれる。本論文は、この帰結を厳密に追跡する試みである。」(Karatani-style hypothetical) - 「〜については、長年〜という解釈が支配的であった。本論文は、この解釈の前提そのものを再検討する。」(Standard challenge-received-view opening) Mẹo về quotation openings — opening với quotation only effective if quotation immediately followed by commentary unpacking its significance. Bare epigraph weak. Mẹo về stakes signaling — implicit signaling preferable to explicit ('this paper is important because...'). Specificity of question + freshness of approach + textual concreteness signal stakes without announcing them. Mẹo về revision tactic — read your opening aloud. Boring? Vague? Confused? Your reader will react similarly. Aural test cuts through writing-fatigue blindness. Mẹo cuối: opening writing is iterative. Don't expect first draft good. Aim for 5-10 revisions of opening across paper-writing process. Effort distribution justified — opening determines reader engagement.",
