    "register_notes": "Defending controversial readings ở C2 Japanese requires sophisticated balance giữa intellectual courage và rhetorical humility. (1) PROOF BURDEN ASYMMETRY — challenges to received view bear higher proof burden than maintaining received view. Cụm: 通説に挑む読みは、通説を提示する論者以上にテクストへの精緻な参照と論理的厳密性を要求される. Must marshal more evidence, more carefully. (2) STRONGEST COUNTER-ARGUMENT INCLUSION — mature controversial paper includes opponent's strongest counter-argument trong its own structure, addresses it. Format: 想定される反論として、〜があり得よう (one anticipated counter-argument is〜); これに対しては、〜と応答することができる (against this, one can respond〜). Failure to anticipate counter-arguments = naive paper. (3) HEDGE STRENGTH OF CLAIM — controversial reading should be presented as 'one possible reading' (一つの読みの可能性) hoặc 'alternative interpretation worth considering' (検討に値する別解釈), không 'definitive correct reading.' Hedge protects from over-extension critique. (4) MULTIPLE CONVERGING EVIDENCE — single decisive evidence rare. Argue from convergence: 〜という複数の細部の収束が、〜という読みを支持する. Multiple weaker evidences > single stronger one (often). (5) FRAME RHETORICALLY — critical: framing same content differently changes reception. 通説を覆す (overturn received view) — aggressive, resistance-inducing; 通説の前提を再検討する (reexamine premises) — humble, dialogue-inducing. Same intellectual content, different rhetorical effect. Choose framing carefully. (6) ENGAGE OPPOSING SCHOLARS BY NAME — naming specific scholars whose readings you challenge required, không vague 'some scholars argue.' Specificity respects opposing scholars while disagreeing. Cụm: 〜氏の読みを最大限に評価しつつ、本論文は〜の点で異なる立場を取る. (7) ACKNOWLEDGE WHAT YOUR READING DOESN'T SOLVE — every reading has costs. Acknowledge: '本論文の読みは〜を説明する反面、〜については別途の検討を要する.' Honest limitation acknowledgment increases credibility. Forbidden moves: 'previous scholars overlooked X' bare claim — implies their incompetence; 'as anyone can see, X' — assumes consensus where none; 'this is the only correct reading' — forecloses dialogue, signals authoritarianism; sneering at opposing readings — destroys credibility regardless of evidence. Required: humility with conviction, evidence with hedge, challenge with respect. Critical writers to study (read their controversial readings as models): 江藤淳 controversial late work on postwar literature; 加藤典洋 'The Postwar of Defeat' political-cultural argument; 大塚英志 controversial otaku-genre thesis; 蓮實重彦 anti-establishment criticism throughout career. Different rhetorical strategies for controversial readings.",
