    "cultural_notes_vi": "Controversial reading defense ở Japanese academic culture có 4 đặc điểm. (1) HIERARCHY SENSITIVITY — challenging senior scholar's reading requires extra rhetorical caution. Junior scholar dismissing 大家 (eminent senior)'s reading directly = career-damaging. Indirect framing essential: 〜氏のご見解を最大限に尊重しつつ、本論文は別の角度から検討を試みる. Same intellectual challenge, less institutional cost. (2) PRIVATE PRE-TESTING — major controversial readings often pre-tested through private circulation among trusted colleagues before public presentation. Refines argument, identifies weak points before exposure. Less common in Anglo-American faster-publication culture. (3) LONG-TIMELINE VINDICATION — Japanese academic memory long. Controversial reading rejected today may be vindicated decades later (江藤淳 wartime literature reading, 桑原武夫 'Second Art' essay on haiku). Controversial position-takers play long game; immediate reception not final verdict. (4) ANCESTRAL DEBATE AWARENESS — many contemporary controversies recapitulate older debates. Knowing previous rounds of debate signals depth, prevents reinventing wheel. C2 critic should know: 私小説 authenticity debate (1920s onward), 純文学/大衆文学 distinction debate (1960s onward), 戦後文学 evaluation debate (1980s-2000s). Khác VN: VN academic culture more politically constrained historically; controversial readings often had political implications. Japanese tradition has its own constraints (especially around 天皇制 references, war responsibility) but generally more space for textual controversy. Mẹo: nếu bạn defend controversial reading, schedule defense talk at 学会 where you're well-known, không where you're stranger. Familiarity creates baseline goodwill that buffers harsh reception. Mẹo về post-presentation follow-up — even after hostile Q&A, send polite follow-up email to dissenting questioners. 本日は貴重なご指摘ありがとうございました。引き続きご教示いただけますと幸いです. Maintains relationship for future. Mẹo về publication strategy — controversial readings sometimes better placed in 評論 (essay) venues than 学術論文 (academic journals). Essay format allows more rhetorical flexibility, less rigid review. Choose venue strategically. Mẹo cuối: controversial readings test your conviction. If you can't defend it under critique, perhaps reading not ready. Iterate privately first; publish when defensive armor solid.",
    "tip_advice_vi": "Workflow defending controversial reading C2 Japanese cho luận văn / book review / conference talk. (a) PRE-VALIDATE WITH 2-3 TRUSTED COLLEAGUES — before public presentation, get feedback from 2-3 senior scholars você trust. Their pre-critique reveals weak points. Adjust before exposure. (b) ASSEMBLE 5-7 CONVERGING EVIDENCES — single decisive evidence rare in interpretive disputes. Marshal 5-7 separate evidences pointing same direction. Convergence builds case. (c) FORMULATE STRONGEST COUNTER-ARGUMENT YOURSELF — không wait cho reviewer. Write strongest argument against your reading IN your paper. Then refute it. Demonstrates intellectual maturity và preempts critique. (d) HEDGE CLAIM SCOPE — present as 'one possible reading' (一つの解釈の可能性), 'alternative worth considering' (検討に値する別解釈), 'reading that opens further discussion' (議論の出発点となり得る読み). Hedged claim harder to refute than absolute claim. (e) CITE OPPOSING SCHOLARS BY NAME WITH RESPECT — 〜氏の読みを最大限に評価しつつ、本論文は〜の点で異なる立場を取る. Specific naming + respect framing makes critique constructive, không personal. (f) ACKNOWLEDGE COSTS OF YOUR READING — every reading has trade-offs. List: 本論文の読みは〜を説明する反面、〜については別途の検討を要する. Honest limitation increases credibility. (g) FRAME RHETORICALLY GENTLE — content can be radical; rhetoric should be moderate. 通説を覆す → 通説の前提を再検討する. Same content, less resistance. Mẹo về citation pattern — controversial-reading paper cite (1) full prior scholarship being challenged (every major proponent), (2) at least one historical precedent for controversial readings in the field (shows you're aware of debate genealogy), (3) theoretical framework licensing your reading, (4) primary text với extensive specific evidence. Quintuple grounding required. Mẹo về Q&A preparation — anticipate 10 hostile questions, prepare 60-second answer for each. Common hostile patterns: 'isn't this against established consensus?' (yes, but consensus deserves reexamination because〜); 'don't you have insufficient evidence?' (multiple convergent evidences as cited); 'isn't your reading reductive?' (no, it adds layer rather than replaces); 'what about counter-passage X?' (acknowledge, explain how reading accommodates). Mẹo về written-defense vs oral-defense distinction — written paper allows full deployment of evidence; oral defense requires distillation. Practice oral version separately. Mẹo về institutional positioning — junior scholars defending controversial reading should make institutional alliance (acknowledge advisor's distinct position, dedicate to teacher who licensed inquiry). Solo controversial scholarship by junior risks isolation. Mẹo cuối: vị trí controversial readings — career-defining when right, career-damaging when wrong. Choose battles. Defending one well-evidenced controversial reading > defending five half-evidenced. Quality > quantity in controversy-mounting.",
